    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear anchor; despite a pending lineup, his projected score of 82.97 against a favorable 4.62 xERA arm makes him the premier play in the order. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused strategy, specifically with **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. His 75.59 score is elevated significantly by a 92% stolen base success probability against the opposing battery, capitalizing on a slow delivery profile to manufacture value in our scarcest category. **Junior Caminero** (70.81) and **Trea Turner** (66.52) round out our high-leverage core, as both benefit from favorable order positioning and positive SP xERA matchups that suggest high run-scoring potential.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the day involved the benching of **Carson Benge**. Despite a decent floor, his 39.99 score fell short due to a stiff matchup against a 3.38 xERA pitcher and a neutral-to-negative platoon split (L/L), causing the optimizer to favor the higher-ceiling profiles of **Colt Keith** and **Lars Nootbaar**. While **Nootbaar** offers a strong 60.52 score, we are monitoring a 42% rain risk that could compromise his plate appearances. Elsewhere, we continue to stash **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds** in the minors, while **Christian Yelich** remains sidelined today due to a lack of a scheduled game. We remain confident that the aggressive deployment of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Trea Turner** will provide the necessary buffer to maintain our efficiency targets across all five categories.",
